A||||2||Knight Rider||Missing Exhaust  Manifold Bolts and Nuts||||1||
Z||000000||Knight Rider||11-10-2001||03:20 PM||||Hey everyone I just bought a 1985 Fiero GT with a rebuilt 2.8 V6.  It has an exhaust leak coming from the front exhaust manifold.  I found that the bolts and nuts that should be on the bottom of each of the exhaust outlets on the stock manifold are missing.  There is a stud on the middle outlet without the nut, but I cannot see what should be on the front outlet.  Could someone with a P22 tell me what the part numbers for these bolts and nuts would be and if the front outlet should be a bolt or a stud and a nut?<P>Thanks,<P>Knight Rider <P> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||11-10-2001||08:39 PM||||on the manifold nearest the front of the car on the top of the manifold there is a stud over #2 and #6 and a bolt over #4. On bottom of the manifold there is a stud under #4 and bolts under #2 and #6. These are mounts for a heat shield.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||11-10-2001||09:22 PM||||find stainless ones at hardware store. and use antisieze coupound on all them. DONT OVERTIGHTEN THEM, OEM ones break very easy. If they break off, you got real problems.||||reg||1
